{
  "meta": {
    "name": "ISMS CORE Chinese termbase (Traditional HK / Simplified)",
    "version": "0.1.0",
    "created": "2026-09-29",
    "scope": "isms-core-framework, -operational, -privacy, -cloud, -ai, -ext, -sec content packs (677 English source documents)",
    "provenance": "Every English key below was harvested from the packs, not invented: field labels occur ~660-670 times each (Document ID, Classification, Status...), section headings up to 188 times (Generator Alignment Reference, Workbook at a Glance). Counts reproducible via tmp/analyze_docs.py.",
    "conventions": {
      "translated": "Section headings, document-control field labels, controlled values (Draft, Internal, Critical...), and all prose. The German tree translates all of these; this termbase follows it.",
      "not_translated": "Framework and standard names, document-ID values in the Document Control table, control identifiers (A.8.9), hex colour codes, file paths, code and data keys.",
      "document_id": "The watermark gains the language suffix (ISMS-OP-POL-A.8.9-ZH-TW) while the Document Control table value stays bare (ISMS-OP-POL-A.8.9). Same rule the de/fr/it trees follow.",
      "path": "<DOCTYPEDIR>/<lang>/<DOCID> - <Translated Title> - <XX>.md",
      "qa_footer": "<!-- QA_VERIFIED: YYYY-MM-DD --> at end of file",
      "language_tags": {
        "primary": {
          "hant": "zh-TW",
          "hans": "zh-CN"
        },
        "rationale": "zh-TW/zh-CN are 5 characters and fit the existing String(5) language column, so no schema migration is needed and the directory convention stays uniform.",
        "alternative": {
          "hant": "zh-Hant",
          "hans": "zh-Hans"
        },
        "alternative_rationale": "BCP-47 correct and script-based rather than region-based, but 7 characters and would need the language column widened. Raised with upstream in issue #4; the pipeline takes --lang so switching is a flag, not a rewrite."
      },
      "variant_choice": "Traditional side targets Hong Kong/Taiwan information-security usage, not mainland-traditional. See variant_note fields: notably 身分 (HK/TW) rather than 身份, and 資料 rather than 數據.",
      "single_character_keys": "A one-character hant key is glossary guidance only; the derivation pass holds it back (see pipeline.derivable). Substitution has no word segmentation to anchor on, so a one-character key fires inside every word containing it — 得 -> 可 rewrote 取得 (to obtain) as 取可. Entries like 得 (may), 欄 (Column) and 應 (shall) stay listed because a translator still needs them; every one of them is glyph-neutral or handled by OpenCC anyway, so derivation is unaffected.",
      "sense_collisions": "A hant key shared by two English senses may not be listed: 重大 is 'material' in 重大變更 and 'Critical' only as a severity value, so mapping it to 严重 rewrote every material change in the corpus as 严重变更. Severity is written 嚴重 on the Traditional side, which OpenCC converts correctly on its own.",
      "substring_hazards": "Substitution is an alternation over raw text with no segmentation, so a multi-character key also fires where its characters merely straddle a word boundary. 範本 (template) is the worked example: it matched inside 僅規範本目錄, where the reading is 規範/本, and the Simplified came out 仅规模板目录. The entry is not wrong and cannot simply be dropped — OpenCC alone turns 範本 into 范本, and 模板 is what a mainland reader needs — so the hazard is inherent to the mechanism and is documented rather than papered over. Two consequences. Whoever drafts the Traditional side should avoid handing a key to the wrong word (the STRUCTURE.md draft was reworded to 僅適用於本目錄). And every derivation should be read once for this class of damage; localization/audit_substrings.py points at the candidates, though it segments with jieba, which is trained on Simplified and therefore over-reports on Traditional text. A sibling case runs the other way — through OpenCC, not the termbase: 登錄 in Taiwan means both 'sign in' and 'registry', OpenCC converts it to 登录 unconditionally, and 私有登錄庫 (private registry) came out 私有登录库. 登錄 gets no entry either, for the same sense-collision reason, so the Traditional side has to write 私有註冊表."
    }
  },
